        <body>
            <div xml:id="d455">

                <pb facs="0808" n="714" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg714"/>

                <head>No. 455.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Manning to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-04-18"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 18, 1887</date>.
                        (Received April 26.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 119.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In connection with my No. 114 of 12th
                    instant, inclosing copy of my note to Mr. Mariscal of same date, calling his
                    attention most earnestly to the alleged discrimination against the American
                    carrying trade, I have now the honor to inclose copy and translation of a note
                    from Mr. Mariscal that reiterates the statement made in his note to me of
                    February 21 last (sent to you under cover of my No. 72, of February 24, 1887),
                    to the effect that he has requested “the department of public works to
                    communicate as soon as possible the data required.”</p>
                <p>While writing this dispatch I have received your No. 77 of April 7, inclosing
                    Alexandre &amp; Sons’ letter to you concerning this alleged discrimination <pb
                        facs="0809" n="715" xml:id="pg715"/> of Mexico against the carrying trade of
                    the United States, and shall promptly communicate to Mr. Mariscal the anxiety
                    felt by Messrs. Alexandre and the Department for a speedy and satisfactory
                    reply.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. C. Manning</hi>.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d455-a1.xml" xpointer="d455-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
